"""Complete microphone-length curves, with separate spoken-response scoring."""
import json
from html import escape as e
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def render(t):
    p=ROOT/'research/s1-array-sweep/review.json'
    if not p.exists():return ''
    d=json.loads(p.read_text());body='<section class="section" id="ami-array-sweep"><h2>Microphone comparisons across all preceding-audio lengths</h2><ul class="brief">'+''.join('<li>'+e(s)+'</li>' for s in d['findings'])+'</ul>'
    body+='<p>Use the same 41 P01 context lengths for each audio signal, from request-only through 309.03 seconds of preceding meeting audio. The raw distant microphone and released eight-microphone beamformed signal use their fixed gains from the level-30 RMS-matched contrast (+16.52 dB and −6.00 dB, respectively) at every length; gain is not retuned across prefixes. All full-prefix peaks remain below clipping. The source boundaries, prompt, greedy decoding, retained history and 40-packet answer window (19.2 seconds of audio packets) are unchanged. The caller enables the first response at the known question end; S2 is disabled. Only the preceding meeting audio changes: the synthetic spoken question keeps its original waveform. The curves therefore measure how preceding microphone audio affects recognition of that later question. As in Figure 1, WER compares S1’s own question-ASR field with the reference question; Parakeet is used separately for the generated responses.</p><p>The original 41 headset outputs, two completed level-30 microphone outputs and identical request-only cases are reused. The extension adds 78 native replays. These are 123 plotted signal/length positions for one question, rather than independent evaluation questions.</p>'
    recordings=json.loads((ROOT/'research/s1-array-sweep/recording-provenance.json').read_text())
    body+='<details id="ami-recording-provenance"><summary>Which AMI recordings and meeting types are used?</summary><p>The original three-request S1 pilot uses the official mono Mix-Headset recordings, which mix the close-talking headsets. P01 and P03 are from TS3006c; P02 is from EN2004a. These are selected question-bank meetings, rather than a named official ASR train/development/test split. The following meeting types come from AMI’s meetings.xml annotations.</p>'
    body+=t('Original S1-pilot source recordings, before synthetic question insertion. Both source WAVs have one channel at 16,000 samples per second.',['Meeting / requests','AMI meeting type','Original source recording'],[[e(r['meeting'])+' / '+e(', '.join(r['pilot_cases'])),e({'scenario':'Scenario meeting','nonscenario':'Non-scenario meeting'}[r['meeting_type']]),'<a href="'+e(r['source_url'])+'">'+e(r['filename'])+'</a>'] for r in recordings['recordings']])
    body+='<p>AMI also releases individual headset signals and distant microphone-array channels for the same meetings. The new contrast changes P01’s preceding TS3006c audio to Array1-01 or the released MDM8 beamformed recording. Array1-01 is one distant channel; the MDM8 WAV is an already combined mono signal from eight microphones. S1 receives a mono waveform in every condition. The inserted question is synthetic speech and is shared across microphone conditions. <a href="https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/download/">AMI signal choices</a> · <a href="research/s1-array-sweep/recording-provenance.json">Recorded source details</a>.</p></details>'
    body+=t('Each curve attempts 41 context lengths; generation failures have no WER score. Eleven lengths per signal contain all reference evidence; only completed responses receive content scores.',['Audio signal','Strict question-ASR passes','LLM complete spoken answers','Source-audited complete spoken answers'],[[e(r['label']),str(r['recognized'])+'/'+str(r['WER_scored'])+' scored; '+str(41-r['WER_scored'])+' unscored',str(r['judge_complete'])+'/'+str(r['judge_scored']),str(r['audited_complete'])+'/'+str(r['audited_scored'])] for r in d['summary']])
    for condition,num,name in [('distant_01',2,'asr-distant'),('beamformed_mdm8',3,'asr-beamformed')]:
        label=next(r['label'] for r in d['summary'] if r['condition']==condition)
        body+='<figure id="array-wer-'+e(condition)+'"><div style="overflow-x:auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="'+e(label)+' ASR curve"><img src="research/s1-array-sweep/'+name+'.svg" alt="Question WER at every original context length for '+e(label)+', with the original headset curve overlaid" style="width:100%;min-width:850px;background:white"></div><figcaption>Figure '+str(num)+'. '+e(label)+' question ASR versus preceding-audio length, using the same word-error-rate calculation as Figure 1. Lower WER is better; an empty question transcript has WER 1. Colors indicate the frozen strict WER/key-term criterion. The dashed gray curve is the original headset result. Red vertical N/A marks denote generation failures, not WER values. The strict ASR rule requires WER at most 0.25 plus the five normalized words assistant, shared, folder, conceptual and design; it is separate from the earlier manual meaning review. <a href="research/s1-array-sweep/'+name+'.svg">SVG</a> · <a href="research/s1-array-sweep/'+name+'.png">PNG</a>.</figcaption></figure>'
    body+='<p><strong>Response-content check:</strong> question WER does not measure transcription or use of the earlier meeting evidence. Independent Parakeet ASR transcribes the actual generated response audio. A separate local Qwen3-30B-A3B-Instruct-2507 judge checks two required facts: that the files/presentations were put in the shared folder, and that the identified file was the components-design PowerPoint. It checks each fact against the candidate answer alone, then separately checks material unsupported claims against the source passages. It receives no microphone label, context length, S1 question-ASR result or prior review. All scored cases are also reviewed against the source by Codex; this is not an independent human rating.</p><p>A response can state zero, one or both facts. The plotted LLM score is the fraction of these two facts stated in the spoken-response transcript. Full correctness additionally requires no material unsupported claim. Shorter prefixes lack the complete reference evidence and are unscored. Generation failures are also unscored. Empty response transcripts receive zero through an explicit guard; nonempty transcripts are checked by the LLM. ASR errors can affect the content score.</p>'
    body+='<p><strong>Automatic-score limitation:</strong> the LLM and Codex source review disagree on '+str(len(d['judge_disagreements']))+' of 33 real responses, mostly in detecting unsupported claims. Figure 4 preserves the raw LLM scores and marks the additional source-review findings. Passing the authored checks does not certify these automatic judgments.</p>'
    body+='<figure id="array-response-content"><div style="overflow-x:auto" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Spoken-response content scores"><img src="research/s1-array-sweep/response-content.svg" alt="Three panels showing the LLM-scored source facts in spoken answers at fully answerable context lengths, with unsupported-claim markers and source-audit corrections" style="width:100%;min-width:850px;background:white"></div><figcaption>Figure 4. LLM content scores on ASR transcripts of actual responses; higher fact count is better. A red cross marks an LLM-flagged material unsupported or contradicted claim; Codex fact-score corrections are hollow diamonds. Open red squares mark additional claims flagged only by Codex source review; their horizontal positions identify the responses, and their heights stay at the LLM fact score. Gray shading marks incomplete reference evidence, not incorrect model answers. One greedy response per position; no error bars or statistical robustness claim. <a href="research/s1-array-sweep/response-content.svg">SVG</a> · <a href="research/s1-array-sweep/response-content.png">PNG</a>.</figcaption></figure>'
    body+='<details id="response-judge-method"><summary>Judge qualification, prompts and limits</summary><p>The first judging attempt failed known-answer checks: it credited an unstated PowerPoint identity and sometimes copied source passages as candidate quotes. Its verdicts were excluded. The revised judge separates candidate-only fact entailment from source factuality and returns candidate sentence IDs so copied text is recovered exactly. '+e(d['judge_qualification_note'])+'</p><p>Exact prompts, raw judge outputs, source-audit findings and the failed qualification remain in the evidence data. Passing these checks does not establish a generally reliable automatic judge. <a href="research/s1-array-sweep/judge-initial-failed-qualification.json">First failed qualification and raw outputs</a>.</p></details>'
    body+='<details id="array-sweep-examples"><summary>Every context length, response transcript, score and actual audio</summary>'
    for s in d['summary']:
        rows=[r for r in d['cases'] if r['condition']==s['condition']];body+='<details><summary>'+e(s['label'])+'</summary>'
        body+=t(s['label']+' exact curve values; content scores are absent when reference evidence is incomplete.',['Level / earlier audio','Question WER','LLM facts / 2','Source audit / 2','Actual response'],[[str(r['index'])+' / '+format(r['context_seconds'],'.2f')+' s',format(r['recognition']['WER'],'.3f') if r['WER_valid'] else 'N/A: generation failure',str(round(r['judge']['fact_score']*2)) if r.get('judge',{}).get('fact_score') is not None else 'N/A',str(round(r['source_audit']['fact_score']*2)) if r.get('source_audit') else 'N/A','<a href="#sweep-'+e(r['id'])+'">Text and audio</a>'] for r in rows])
        for r in rows:
            if not r['response_valid']:
                body+='<details id="sweep-'+e(r['id'])+'"><summary>Level '+str(r['index'])+' · '+format(r['context_seconds'],'.2f')+' seconds · unscored</summary><p>'+e(r.get('error') or r['status'])+'</p><p>This attempt did not complete the native input/answer sequence. It has no answer-content score; question WER is also unscored if the full recognition window was not reached.</p></details>'
                continue
            body+='<details id="sweep-'+e(r['id'])+'"><summary>Level '+str(r['index'])+' · '+format(r['context_seconds'],'.2f')+' seconds</summary><p><strong>Question ASR:</strong> '+e(r['question_asr'] or '(empty)')+'</p><p><strong>Native response text:</strong> '+e(r['speech_text'] or '(empty)')+'</p><audio controls preload="none" src="'+e(r['audio'])+'" aria-label="'+e(s['label'])+' level '+str(r['index'])+' actual response"></audio><p><strong>Independent response transcript:</strong> '+e(r['spoken_transcript'] or '(empty)')+'</p>'
            if r.get('source_audit'):body+='<p>'+e(r['source_audit']['reason'])+'</p>'
            body+='</details>'
        body+='</details>'
    body+='</details><p>Each S1 worker uses one H100 SXM 80 GB: Thinker, Talker, MTP and Code2Wav share GPU 0, followed by independent Parakeet ASR after S1 shuts down. Workers have private services; cases within each worker are sequential fresh sessions. The text judge uses one H100 SXM 80 GB separately, with weights and KV cache on GPU 0 and no S1/ASR sharing. '+e(d['resource_note'])+'</p><p><strong>Limits:</strong> one question, one greedy replay per signal/length, controlled answer start and an unpaced response window. Released AMI beamforming is offline and may use later-audio statistics. Neither these curves nor the judge qualification validates the full 105-question study.</p><p><a href="research/s1-array-sweep/review.json">Reviewed curve data and source examples</a> · <a href="research/s1-array-sweep/curve-values.csv">Exact values (CSV)</a> · <a href="research/s1-array-sweep/judge-results.json">LLM judgments and qualification</a> · <a href="research/s1-array-sweep/manifest.json">Checksums</a></p></section>'
    return body
